  "id": "Compound::DB00622 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Nicardipine, a dihydropyridine calcium channel blocker, is linked to Cyp2b6 through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Nicardipine binds to Cyp2b6, as indicated by direct interaction in Path 1 and Path 3, and through indirect pathways involving Cyp2c19, which is part of the arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity, which is also associated with Cyp2b6. This creates a network of interactions where Nicardipine is indirectly linked to Cyp2b6 via Cyp2c19 and its downstream activity. The lowest common ancestors in the paths further reinforce the shared classification of Nicardipine and Nifedipine within the same family, highlighting a structural and functional link. The integration of these pathways suggests that Nicardipine may influence Cyp2b6 through metabolic or enzymatic pathways, potentially affecting drug metabolism or other biological processes.",
